IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pipa-dates`
IMPORT `pipa-claimant`

-- Personal Injuries Proceedings Act 2002 (Queensland) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (pipa-claimant.l4)
-- and the date helpers (pipa-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied
-- from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts
-- are illustrative. The offer limits in the s 56 cases (lower $50,000, upper $100,000) are invented: the Minister's
-- notice under s 75A is not deposited.
-- Day counts used: 60 days after 10 September 2026 is 9 November 2026 (20 days to 30 September, 31 in October, 9 in
-- November); 60 days after 15 July 2026 is 13 September 2026 (16 + 31 + 13); 60 days after 1 October 2026 is
-- 30 November 2026 (30 + 30); 7 days after 25 February 2026 is 4 March 2026 (2026 is not a leap year); 7 days after
-- 25 December 2026 is 1 January 2027; 14 days after 20 December 2026 is 3 January 2027.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

`ordinary` MEANS `ordinary claim`
`abuse` MEANS `abuse as a child`
`medical` MEANS `medical incident under s 9A`

`in time` MEANS `in time: I give it by the last day`
`late` MEANS `late: the duty to give it continues, and I must give a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 9(5), s 9A(6))`
`excused` MEANS `late, but I am taken to have a reasonable excuse because of my health service complaint (s 9(6), s 9A(6A))`
`no limit` MEANS `no time limit: s 9(3), (5) and (6) do not apply to a claim for abuse as a child (s 9(9C))`
`not fixed` MEANS `no day fixed yet: part 1 for a medical incident is due 12 months after the respondent answers my initial notice (s 9A(9)(b))`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the date` 9 `months after` (`d` 14 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 14 12 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 9 `months after` (`d` 31 5 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 1 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 72 `months after` (`d` 1 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `months after` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2027
#ASSERT `the day` 60 `days after` (`d` 10 9 2026) EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 7 `days after` (`d` 25 2 2026) EQUALS `d` 4 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day` (-7) `days after` (`d` 5 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 26 2 2026
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (`d` 1 5 2026) `and` (`d` 14 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 5 2026
#ASSERT `the later of` (`d` 1 5 2026) `and` (`d` 14 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 14 12 2026
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 10 9 2026) `to` (`d` 9 11 2026) EQUALS 60

§§ `The regulative rules, run directly`

-- s 40(4): the offer is open through day 14; starting on day 14 breaks the bar, day 15 does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` `s 40(4) -- not while the offer is open` `I` `start my court proceeding` 14)
#ASSERT `the rule is met` `s 40(4) -- not while the offer is open` `I` `start my court proceeding` 15
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` `s 40(4) -- not while the offer is open` `I` `start my court proceeding` 0)
-- s 42: the last of 60 days is in time, the 61st is not.
#ASSERT `the rule is met` (`s 42 -- start within the time` 60) `I` `start my court proceeding` 60
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` (`s 42 -- start within the time` 60) `I` `start my court proceeding` 61)
-- s 9(3), (5): late, the rule is not met (the excuse is then owed).
#ASSERT `the rule is met` (`s 9(3), (5) -- give part 1 in time, or with an excuse` 275) `I` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` 275
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` (`s 9(3), (5) -- give part 1 in time, or with an excuse` 275) `I` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` 276)
-- s 22: a step by the wrong party does not meet it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` (`s 22 -- give the documents or information` 31) `the respondent` `give the documents or information` 10)
#ASSERT `the rule is met` (`s 22 -- give the documents or information` 31) `I` `give the documents or information` 31
-- s 20C: the parent's notice.
#ASSERT `the rule is met` (`s 20C(1), 20D -- my parent gives part 1 in time` 100) `my parent or legal guardian` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` 100
#ASSERT NOT (`the rule is met` (`s 20C(1), 20D -- my parent gives part 1 in time` 100) `my parent or legal guardian` `give part 1 of my notice of claim` 101)

§§ `s 6 -- whether the Act applies to my injury`

#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `a personal injury not covered by any of the other choices` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act applies to my personal injury (s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `a personal injury not covered by any of the other choices` TRUE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to an injury for which a proceeding was started in a court before 18 June 2002 (s 6(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `an injury from a motor vehicle to which the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 applies` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to a motor vehicle injury under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (s 6(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `a work injury, and I seek damages from my employer under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to my damages claim against my employer; the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 chapter 5 regulates it (s 6(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `an injury to which an earlier scheme named in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies, to the extent stated there` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to the extent an earlier scheme in s 6(2)(b) or (d) to (g) applies`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `a dust-related condition` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to a dust-related condition (s 6(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury` `a claim for financial assistance or damages under a scheme named in s 6(5), such as the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009` FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not affect a claim under the schemes in s 6(5); that scheme governs it`

§§ `s 9 -- to whom I give my notices`

#ASSERT `To whom must I give my notice` `part 1 of my notice of claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the person against whom I propose to start the proceeding (s 9(1), s 9A(2))`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my notice` `part 1 of my notice of claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Crown solicitor, and part 1 must identify the government department or entity I consider responsible (s 9(8))`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my notice` `my initial notice for a medical incident` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the health service chief executive of the Hospital and Health Service that controls the place (s 9A(7)(a))`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my notice` `my initial notice for a medical incident` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the chief executive officer of the department or entity that controls the place of the medical incident (s 9A(7)(b))`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my notice` `my initial notice for a medical incident` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the person against whom I propose to start the proceeding (s 9(1), s 9A(2))`

§§ `ss 9(3), 9A(4), 19 -- by when I give part 1 or the initial notice`

-- A fall on 14 March 2026, symptoms at once, no lawyer: 9 months on.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 14 12 2026)
-- A lawyer instructed on 1 April 2026, the respondent known that day: 1 month on, earlier than 9 months.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 5 2026)
-- The respondent identified only on 20 May 2026: 1 month from then (fork F4).
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 20 5 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 20 6 2026)
-- A lawyer instructed after the 9 months ran: the 9-month day is earlier.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 2 2027) (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 14 12 2026)
-- Instructed on 31 January 2026: 1 month on is the last day of February.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 31 1 2026) (`d` 31 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2026)
-- Symptoms not immediately apparent; first seen 31 May 2026: 9 months on, end of February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 31 5 2026) FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2027)
-- Injured as a child on 10 January 2020, 18 on 5 June 2026 (s 19): 9 months from the end of the disability.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 2020) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` TRUE (`d` 5 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 5 3 2027)
-- The same, a lawyer instructed while still a child: the 1-month limb also starts when the disability ends (fork F5).
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 2020) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 5 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 5 7 2026)
-- Abuse as a child: no period (s 9(9C)).
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `abuse` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 1995) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Medical incident: 12 months after the respondent's s 9A(8) answer; none fixed before it answers.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` TRUE (`d` 10 4 2026) (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 12 2025) (`d` 1 12 2025) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 4 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 14 3 2027) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The initial notice: the same counting from the medical incident.
#ASSERT `By when must I give my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 14 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 2 4 2026) (`d` 2 4 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 2 5 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 1 5 2027

§§ `ss 9(5), 9(6), 9A(6), 9A(6A) -- if I am late`

-- Part 1 due 14 December 2026: on the day, the day after, and with a health service complaint.
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 12 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `excused`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 12 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
-- With a lawyer instructed 1 April 2026: due 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 2 5 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late`
-- A child, 18 on 5 June 2026: due 5 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 2020) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` TRUE (`d` 5 6 2026) (`d` 5 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `ordinary` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 2020) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` TRUE (`d` 5 6 2026) (`d` 6 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late`
-- Abuse as a child: no time limit, even decades on.
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `abuse` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 1 1985) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
-- Medical incident: the respondent answered on 10 April 2026, so part 1 is due 10 April 2027.
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` TRUE (`d` 10 4 2026) (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 4 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` TRUE (`d` 10 4 2026) (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 11 4 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Am I late with part 1 of my notice of claim` `medical` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 11 4 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not fixed`
-- The initial notice, due 14 December 2026.
#ASSERT `Am I late with my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I late with my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Am I late with my initial notice` (`d` 14 3 2026) TRUE `unused` FALSE `unused` `unused` FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 12 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `excused`

§§ `ss 9(3A), 10, 13 -- by when I give part 2`

-- Part 1 received 10 March 2026; the person has until 10 April 2026 to respond.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` (`d` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` (`d` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 6 2026
-- A response on 11 April 2026 is late; the presumption arose that day (fork F6).
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` (`d` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 11 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 11 6 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` (`d` 10 3 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 11 6 2026
-- Received 31 January 2026, no response: the time to respond ends 28 February, presumption 1 March, part 2 by 1 May.
#ASSERT `By when must I give part 2 of my notice of claim` (`d` 31 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 1 5 2026

§§ `ss 13, 18 -- whether I can go on`

#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my part 1 is a complying part 1 notice of claim`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent stated it is satisfied with part 1, or that I have taken reasonable action to remedy it (s 18(1)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent did not respond in time and is conclusively presumed satisfied (s 13, s 18(1)(a)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent waived compliance (s 18(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court declared that I remedied the noncompliance, or authorised me to proceed, on any conditions it set (s 18(1)(c), (2))`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim after part 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my failure to give a complying part 1 notice prevents me from proceeding further with the claim (s 18(1))`

§§ `div 1A -- a child injured by medical treatment`

-- The parent knew on 1 March 2020 and consulted no lawyer: before 1 March 2026, so the last day is 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2026)
-- Consulted a lawyer on 1 June 2024: before 1 December 2025, so 30 November 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST (`d` 30 11 2025)
-- Consulted late, so the 6-year day is earlier.
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2026)
-- Knew on 29 February 2020: 6 years on is 28 February 2026 (fork F2), so the last day is 27 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` TRUE TRUE (`d` 29 2 2020) FALSE `unused` EQUALS JUST (`d` 27 2 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must my parent give part 1 for my medical treatment injury` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` EQUALS NOTHING
-- What follows a late notice.
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` (`d` 28 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time: my parent gives part 1 by the last day under s 20C`
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late: the respondent may apply for an order that my claim not proceed (s 20D); the court decides on the justice of the case (s 20E); if the application is dismissed, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20F)`
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `late after a notice of an adverse event: part 1 can be given only with the court's leave, and I must show why the claim should proceed (s 20H, 20I); if leave is given, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20J)`
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 1 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS `late after a notice of an adverse event: part 1 can be given only with the court's leave, and I must show why the claim should proceed (s 20H, 20I); if leave is given, I can not recover my parent's costs and gratuitous services for the time before part 1, unless the court orders otherwise (s 20J)`
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2024) (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE EQUALS `in time: my parent gives part 1 by the last day under s 20C`
#ASSERT `What follows a late notice for my medical treatment injury as a child` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered: division 1A applies only to a claim for a child's injury from medical treatment (s 20B)`

§§ `s 22 -- what I must give the respondent, and by when`

#ASSERT `By when must I give the respondent documents or information` `copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give the respondent documents or information` `a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later` (`d` 25 2 2026) EQUALS `d` 4 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give the respondent documents or information` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give the respondent documents or information` `telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances` (`d` 31 10 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 11 2026
-- What follows.
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: nothing follows`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late, without proper reason: I am liable for the respondent's costs resulting from the failure (s 22(8)), and the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2026) `unused` TRUE EQUALS `late, with a proper reason: no liability for costs under s 22(8), but the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 30 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time: nothing follows`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `an answer to the respondent's request for information` (`d` 31 3 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late, without proper reason: I am liable for the respondent's costs resulting from the failure (s 22(8)), and the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 2 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: nothing follows`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `copies of reports and material I held when I gave notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 16 2 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35), and I can not use an undisclosed document in a later court proceeding unless the court orders otherwise (s 32)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later` (`d` 25 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 4 3 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: nothing follows`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `a copy of a report or material that came into my possession later` (`d` 25 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 5 3 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35), and I can not use an undisclosed document in a later court proceeding unless the court orders otherwise (s 32)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances` (`d` 31 10 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late: the court may order me to remedy it, with costs (s 35)`
#ASSERT `What follows if I do not give documents or information in time` `telling the respondent of a change in my condition or circumstances` (`d` 31 10 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: nothing follows`

§§ `ss 23-25 -- expert reports and examinations`

#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` TRUE TRUE 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not this section: I agreed to an expert report, so it is a joint arrangement under s 23`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must undergo the examination or assessment, with a doctor or expert I select from the respondent's panel, at the respondent's expense (s 25(2))`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must undergo the examination or assessment, with a doctor or expert I select from the respondent's panel, at the respondent's expense (s 25(2))`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I am not obliged, because it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious (s 25(3))`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE FALSE 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
#ASSERT `Must I undergo the examination the respondent asks for` FALSE TRUE 4 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the request does not meet s 25(2): it must be at the respondent's expense and let me choose from a panel of at least 3 (or 2, if 3 suitable doctors or experts are not available)`
#ASSERT `Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent must reimburse my reasonable cost of the report, on my request (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as our agreement says: my right is subject to its terms, and they deal with the cost (s 24(2))`
#ASSERT `Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 24 gives no right unless the report was obtained by agreement, I am liable for its cost, and I ask (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 24 gives no right unless the report was obtained by agreement, I am liable for its cost, and I ask (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Must the respondent reimburse my expert report` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 24 gives no right unless the report was obtained by agreement, I am liable for its cost, and I ask (s 24(1))`

