§§ `s 42 -- by when I should start my court proceeding`

#ASSERT `By when should I start my court proceeding` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
-- Dispensed with on 1 March 2026; part 1 given 15 January 2026: 60 days after 15 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court proceeding` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 13 9 2026
-- Dispensed with on 1 October 2026: 60 days after that date, the later.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court proceeding` TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `d` 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court proceeding` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2026
-- Starting late.
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 9 11 2026) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: I start within the time in s 42`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `unused` TRUE EQUALS `late, but not prevented: I have a reasonable excuse, so no costs order for the delay under s 42(4)(a); the court may still fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 12 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `barred: I did not start within the time limit the court fixed under s 42(4)(b) (s 42(5)), despite the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (s 42(6))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 13 9 2026) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: I start within the time in s 42`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 9 2026) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2026) (`d` 31 12 2026) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `in time: I start within the time in s 42`
#ASSERT `What happens if I start my proceeding late` FALSE (`d` 10 9 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2026) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE `unused` FALSE EQUALS `late, but not prevented: the court may order me to pay the respondent's costs of the delay, unless I establish a reasonable excuse, and may fix a time limit on a respondent's application (s 42(4))`

§§ `ss 43, 44 -- starting an urgent proceeding`

#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding urgently` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave, and it is not stayed: Part 1 (other than s 43), ss 48, 56 and 59 and chapter 4 no longer apply to my injury (s 43(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding urgently` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 43(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding urgently` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, because every proposed respondent agreed, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 44(8))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding urgently` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, because every proposed respondent agreed, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 or it ends (s 44(8))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding urgently` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: without the court's leave or every proposed respondent's agreement, I must first give notice of my claim and hold the compulsory conference (s 9(1), s 36(1))`
#ASSERT `By when must the respondent answer my urgent request` (`d` 25 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 1 2027

§§ `s 59 -- starting after the limitation period`

-- Limitation period ends 14 March 2029; complying part 1 given 1 March 2029: 6 months on is 1 September 2029.
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 9 2029) EQUALS `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 2 9 2029) EQUALS `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` FALSE (`d` 1 9 2029) EQUALS `yes, but the proceeding is stayed until I comply with Part 1 (s 59(3)): my complying part 1 was given in time and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 14 3 2029) EQUALS `the limitation period has not ended when I start: s 59 is not needed`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 15 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2029) EQUALS `no: s 59 does not help, because my complying part 1 notice was not given before the limitation period ended`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 14 3 2029) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2029) EQUALS `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
-- Leave granted 1 June 2029: 6 months from the leave (fork F12).
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2029) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 1 12 2029) EQUALS `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2029) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 2 12 2029) EQUALS `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`
-- A longer period to 31 December 2029.
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 31 12 2029) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2029) EQUALS `yes: my complying part 1 notice was given before the limitation period ended, and I start within the time in s 59(2)`
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 31 12 2029) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`
-- Part 1 given 31 August 2028: 6 months on is 28 February 2029, before the limitation period ends; starting after it ends is too late.
#ASSERT `Can I start my proceeding after the limitation period` (`d` 14 3 2029) (`d` 31 8 2028) FALSE `unused` FALSE `unused` TRUE (`d` 15 3 2029) EQUALS `no: I start after the time s 59(2) allows (6 months after part 1 or leave, or the longer period the court allowed)`

§§ `ss 6(4), 43(5), 56 -- costs`

`low` MEANS 50000
`high` MEANS 100000

#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 40000 `low` `high` 45000 30000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs are awarded either way (s 56(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 45000 `low` `high` 45000 30000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to me on an indemnity basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 30000 `low` `high` 45000 30000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to the respondent on a standard basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 50000 `low` `high` 60000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs are awarded either way (s 56(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 50001 `low` `high` 60000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to me on a standard basis, up to the declared costs limit (s 56(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 100000 `low` `high` 90000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and on an indemnity basis from that day (s 56(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 70000 `low` `high` 80000 70000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to me on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before the proceeding started, and to the respondent on a standard basis from that day (s 56(3)(c))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 100001 `low` `high` 90000 40000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 56 does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit (s 56(1))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 40000 `low` `high` 45000 30000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 56 does not apply: the injury came from an unlawful intentional act done to cause injury, or unlawful sexual assault or misconduct (s 6(4))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 40000 `low` `high` 45000 30000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 56 does not apply: my urgent proceeding was not stayed (s 43(5)(b))`
-- My offer below the respondent's: an award between them meets (b) and (c); (b) is taken (fork F13).
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 42000 `low` `high` 40000 45000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `costs to me on an indemnity basis from the day the proceeding started, and none before it (s 56(2)(b))`
-- The respondent denied liability and offered $nil.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs if I am awarded no more than the upper offer limit` 20000 `low` `high` 30000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs are awarded either way (s 56(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest for the time I was in default` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not affected: I complied with the notice requirements (part 1, division 1)`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest for the time I was in default` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possible: the court may award me interest for the period I was in default, as it is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest for the time I was in default` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the court may not award me interest for the period I was in default without a reasonable excuse (s 48(1)(b)); it may also award the respondent its costs caused by my default (s 48(1)(a))`
